# UI Interactions

Apply when building buttons, menus, cards, or any interactive UI:

## Reuse

- Search for existing shared primitives, hooks, or CSS classes before creating new ones.
- Extract repeated interaction logic into a shared component or hook.

## Motion & Sound

- Use `<motion.button>` / `<motion.a>` with `whileHover={{ scale: 1.05 }}` and `whileTap={{ scale: 0.95 }}`.
- Import sounds from `src/lib/sound/interactionSounds.ts` — no external audio assets.
- Wire `playHoverSound` on `onMouseEnter`, `playClickSound` on `onClick`.
- Fire `playMenuCloseSound` on every menu/modal dismiss path (close button, backdrop, nav links).

## Accessibility

- Never put `onClick` on `<div>` or `<span>` — use semantic `<button>` or `<a>`.
- Add `aria-label` to icon-only buttons.

Load `.cursor/skills/frontend/ui-interactions/SKILL.md` for implementation examples.
